  249|       |   /* There are four flags two for ancillary and two for critical chunks.  The
  250|       |    * default setting of these flags is all zero.
  251|       |    *
  252|       |    * PNG_FLAG_CRC_ANCILLARY_USE
  253|       |    * PNG_FLAG_CRC_ANCILLARY_NOWARN
  254|       |    *  USE+NOWARN: no CRC calculation (implemented here), else;
  255|       |    *  NOWARN:     png_chunk_error on error (implemented in png_crc_finish)
  256|       |    *  else:       png_chunk_warning on error (implemented in png_crc_finish)
  257|       |    *              This is the default.
  258|       |    *
  259|       |    *    I.e. NOWARN without USE produces png_chunk_error.  The default setting
  260|       |    *    where neither are set does the same thing.
  261|       |    *
  262|       |    * PNG_FLAG_CRC_CRITICAL_USE
